---
// The root serves the tool itself — the standalone tool's "homepage" IS the
// separator tool, rendered as one page on two routes. The page's canonical
// points at /separators/, the tool's true home and the path every bookmark URL
// uses, so search engines see a single page.
//
// This MUST stay a real render, never a redirect: Chrome attributes favicon
// updates from a client-redirected document to every same-document URL the
// page passes through, so a meta-refresh here let the live color re-tint
// overwrite freshly dragged bookmarks' frozen favicons (verified against
// Chrome's Favicons DB). Server redirects (e.g. a host's trailing-slash 301)
// are unaffected. The private site replaces this route with its homepage.
import SeparatorsPage from './separators/index.astro';
---

<SeparatorsPage />
